WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.234 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-And finally, New Rule.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.903 line:0%
Now that I've heard
author Michael Lewis say

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.004 line:0%
about his latest subject

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.240 line:0%
crypto crasher,
Sam Bankman-Fried,

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:11.211 line:0%
that... (READS PROMPT)

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:22.489 line:0%
-(SMACKS LIPS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.858 line:0%
I say we finally start
seriously looking at what phones

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.693 line:0%
are doing to people's brains.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.663 line:0%
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING,
CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.765
Wow.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.770
And not just phones,

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.073
there has been a perfect storm
of events in recent years

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:43.776
that has led the surgeon general
of the United States

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.312
to issue an advisory that
America is suffering from...

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:51.284 line:0%
(READS PROMPT)

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.920 line:0%
What Matt Gaetz calls
"another day at work."

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.957
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.727
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:05.998
And this is not just in America,
Japan and the UK

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.734
have actually appointed
a cabinet level position

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.203
for Minister for Loneliness...

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.373
because the studies and the data
from around the world

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.941
show that
the health consequences

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:18.511
of so many people
feeling so isolated

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.679
are staggering.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:23.349
Skyrocketing rates of stroke,
heart disease, premature death.

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:26.552
It's just become too easy
to isolate now.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.088
We've got our phones
and our gadgets to distract

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.123
from having
an actual conversation.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.893
Amazon to deliver
instead of going to a store.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.129
Grubhub instead of going
to a restaurant.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.931
Movies streaming on TV
instead of going to a theater.

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:42.669
And even when we do go out,
the earbuds stay in.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.803
(AUDIENCE CHUCKLING)

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.272
We can't even do
casual chitchat anymore.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.441
Remember when you'd roll
through the checkout line

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.110
with a six-pack
and a box of condoms. (SNICKERS)

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.579
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:56.416
-(CHUCKLES)
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.818
You know.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.889
You'd have a little moment
with the checker

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:03.857
where he'd be like...

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.725
"Heh.
Somebody's having a party, huh?"

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.360
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(CHUCKLES)

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:11.330
But there are no high fives
at the self-checkout.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.533
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.002
We've traded going out
with people we like

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.471
for going on Facebook
to get likes.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:23.042
Has anything ever been
more misnamed than social media?

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.111
It's done more
to kill being social

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.648
-than the pocket protector.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.085
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.988
It should be called,
"Antisocial media."

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:39.459
And then AI came along
and made it even worse.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.061
Do you know a 19-year-old
from Southampton, England

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.597
recently breached the walls
of Windsor Castle

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.200
in an attempt
to assassinate the Queen

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.436
because
his AI chatbot girlfriend

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.405
told him it would impress her?

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.541
Yes,
there's an AI Jodie Foster now.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:58.777
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING,
APPLAUDING)

00:02:58.877 --> 00:02:59.946
(SCOFFS)

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:07.086
And the idea
that your "girlfriend"

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.488
now is just a voice
in your phone

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:14.159
just like in that movie,<i> Her,</i>
is no longer science fiction.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.130
There's one bot chick
on the market called "Replika"

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.132
and she has two million users,

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:21.901
and boy is she gonna be
in trouble

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.236
when her boyfriends find out

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.837
she's seeing
two million other guys.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:28.608
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING,
CHEERING)

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:36.148
Everybody keeps saying
how AI is coming for your job,

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.216
and it may well be,

00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:38.851
but it's also coming
for your boyfriend.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.387
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(SMACKS LIPS)

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.724
Yuval Harari asked the question
about the future...

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:48.795
(READS PROMPT)

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:55.334
I don't know but it sounds like
it'll be a profitable world

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.102
for the makers of Jergens.

00:03:57.202 --> 00:04:03.743
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING,
CHEERING)

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.912
And if the technology

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:08.848
wasn't making the problem
bad enough,

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:12.184
we also have a media
that is built on ginning up fear

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.888
and hostility, and convincing us
no place is ever really safe.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.224
Poor Britney Spears
can't even dance in her own home

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.061
-without a couple of knives.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:23.896
AUDIENCE MEMBER: Whoo!

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:31.036
We've become like that old lady
from<i> The Twilight Zone</i> episode

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.971
who hides behind closed doors

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:35.307
because she thinks
death is trying to get in.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:36.642
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.544
But here's the irony
in real life,

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:42.281
what's killing you
may well be you staying inside.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:45.652
The overreaction
to the COVID pandemic

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:49.021
may turn out to be more damaging
than the disease itself.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.457
The strategy
of social distancing

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:54.460
and staying home to work,
and staying home from school

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.196
all for very long periods
of time

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.398
made us into different people.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.835
Safetyism became
a political identity,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.804
and now some people never want
to go back to work

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.140
or school or Venezuela.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:14.614
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING,
APPLAUDING)

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.718
Too many people
got used to saying,

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:22.154
"No, I can't make it
to your birthday party.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.455
Not for any compelling reason,

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:25.457
just for the sake
of ultimate safety."

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:29.094
Well, we're just now starting
to tally the collateral damage

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:32.264
from ultimate safety,
from long lockdowns

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.834
and creating
four-year-old germaphobes,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:38.304
and they include
erasing two decades of progress

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.705
in math and reading.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.708
School absenteeism
as the new normal.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.645
An all-time drug high
and overdoses and murders.

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:49.381
Huge increases in obesity
and depression

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:51.216
and the atrophying
of social skills

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:52.284
that lead to it.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.586
You know what else
went off the charts

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:56.722
the last couple of years?
Car crashes.

00:05:57.022 --> 00:06:00.193
They couldn't figure out why.
You know what they came up with?

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.227
People's heads
are just so scrambled,

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:03.830
and they're so full
of pent-up rage

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.931
from being locked up
and the kids home all the time,

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:07.399
and my stupid fucking husband.

00:06:07.499 --> 00:06:09.568
So, they just got in the car
and drove like a maniac,

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:13.306
-and took it out on the road.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.777
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING)
-So... (CHUCKLES)

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.882
So, to quote every mother
since the dawn of time,

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.651
for fuck's sake,
go play outside.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:28.387
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, CHEERING,
APPLAUDING)

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.455
Huh?

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.460
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.196
I know, I know.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.900
Outside is full of flashers
and rusty nails

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:43.469
and germs and sharks
and stranger danger.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.270
-(AUDIENCE CHUCKLING)
-But your mother was right,

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:47.873
it's actually worse
to stay cooped up.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.609
Magazine surveys
like to ask the question,

00:06:50.675 --> 00:06:51.977
"How would you like to die?"

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:55.647
My answer is, "Anything
except going unnoticed

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.950
until the neighbors complain
about the smell."

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.454
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING,
CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:07:06.258 --> 00:07:09.061
Twenty years ago, the show
that defined the Zeitgeist

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:12.799
was called<i> Friends.</i>
Today, it's<i> Naked and Afraid.</i>

